*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Exceptions — stored as ordinary git blobs, NOT LFS pointers.
#
# A host that clones the repo without fetching LFS (Railway does not) sees a
# ~130 byte pointer file instead of the image. For app/icon.png and
# app/apple-icon.png that fails the build outright: Next's metadata image loader
# reports "unsupported file type: undefined". The rest are small assets the
# running site needs, which would otherwise be served as 130 bytes of pointer
# text. Total here is ~240 KB, so keeping them out of LFS costs nothing.
#
# Large binaries (public/gallery, public/catalogues) deliberately stay in LFS.
app/icon.png !filter !diff !merge
app/apple-icon.png !filter !diff !merge
public/RG-Tech-Logo.png !filter !diff !merge
public/ai-logos/*.png !filter !diff !merge
